# Derived by hand from Type System ch. 5 (a `u fn` takes its color from its call; the function the returned function gives is the one made of the one passed) and Semantics ch. 7 (a cycle point sits "at every call of an unbounded function from an unbounded function, whether the callee is named, a lambda, or a function whose color variable is instantiated unbounded at that call"): entering `Through` and its call of `Make`, an unbounded lambda, are two cycles, as sem-ch07-calls-in-branches has an entry and one call; the call of `Maker` stands in the widget's line and `Add` is bounded. 5 + 1 + 2 at tick 2.
